"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act4_ch20.md — do not edit */

SC["a4c20_open"]={t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER TWENTY — THE FRAYED HEAVEN`)+P(`Winter takes the lake country the way sleep takes a tired man: all at once, and deeper than expected. The river hardens at its edges. The chandler's loft above Wan's Fine Cordage — Bao's network made flesh, three rooms of rope-smell and letter-boxes — becomes the closest thing you have had to a home since the kitchens.`)+P(`The tribute-rolls work all winter without you. That's the strange mercy of paper: you sleep, and somewhere downriver a magistrate Yan's office wrote to is freezing a granary account, and a hall that fed a furnace for a decade is explaining its arithmetic to men with seals. Eleven halls. Four have already published confessions of “irregular donations.” Two have burned their own records, which is also an answer.`)+P(`And on a beloved shoulder, all winter, the white thread does the only thing it does. It points.`)+((G.f.a3_marked=="sho")?(P(`Granny Sho sits by the loft's small stove most evenings, cane across her knees, and the thread on her shoulder lies flat and fine and always, always angled upriver, like a compass needle that has chosen its north and is patient about it. She will not let you study it more than once a week. “It's a claim, boy, not a riddle. You don't learn a debt by staring at the notice. You learn it by visiting the creditor.”`)):(P(`Ruan has taken to wearing the thread the way he wears everything: audited. He measured its angle against the loft's beams on the first of every month — upriver, always upriver, one degree westerly as the season turned, which he noted in the margin of his book as if it were a grain price. “It knows where it's going,” he said, the third month, quietly. “I'd rather we arrived before it expects us, brother.”`))),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Spring opens the river. The letters come up with the first boats.`,go:"a4c20_letters"}]};

SC["a4c20_letters"]={t:()=>P(`Three letters, one morning, with the ice barely out of the bays.`)+P(`Yan Shuo's is formal to the bone and warmer than it knows: the sect's auditors have petitioned the regional alliance for a JOINT INQUEST into “irregularities of tribute” across the watershed, and the petition names, as its evidentiary basis, rolls recovered by “an itinerant auditor of prior acquaintance.” <i>The inquest will travel,</i> he writes. <i>I have asked to carry the writ. Do not conclude your business before honor can arrive to witness it.</i>`)+P(`Bao's is grease-spotted and twice as long, food in every metaphor: the network fat and happy, the chandler accounts cooking nicely, a new contact in the silk trade who talks about the upper lake “like a man describing the inside of a steamed bun — white, soft, and you'll never guess what it's wrapped around.” At the bottom, smaller: <i>The Court buys stories about you. I've started selling them — the wrong ones. Cheap. Forgive me the lying, it's the most honest work I've ever done.</i>`)+((G.f.a3_mei_present)?(P(`Mei doesn't send a letter. Mei sends a crate: salves, tinctures, a sewn packet labeled FOR BURNS in her square hand, and at the bottom, wrapped in oilcloth, a sprig of something green and impossible in the first week of spring. She arrives two days behind it, walks up the loft stairs as if she'd left yesterday, looks at you for a long moment over the crate you haven't finished unpacking, and says: “You've been sleeping badly. Sit. I'll make tea, and you'll tell me what heaven did to deserve you.”`)):(P(`Mei's letter is four lines, square-handed, no greeting: <i>The clinic stands. The mountain sends fewer broken servants since you audited it. I have learned the burn-salve recipe well enough to teach it. If you go where I think you are going, golden boy, go stitched.</i>`))),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The fourth letter has no sender, white paper, needle-fine hand.`,go:"a4c20_invite"}]};

SC["a4c20_invite"]={t:()=>P(`It is not a letter. It is an itinerary.`)+P(`<i>The thaw stands at six days. The white boat calls at the Patient Heron on the first of the fourth month. The Lady of the Reels anticipates the pleasure. — X.</i>`)+P(`No threat. No terms. The Court does not negotiate the way other powers negotiate, because the Court has never once believed it was negotiating: it sets the table, names the hour, and waits for the river to deliver you, because the river always has.`)+P(`Ruan reads it twice, sets it down, and aligns its edge with the table's edge, which is what he does instead of swearing. “She gives us the date of our own arrival,” he says. “Fine bookkeeping. I'd admire it from further away.”`)+((G.f.a3_marked=="sho")?(P(`Granny Sho laughs her dry-leaves laugh from the stove corner. “Six days of thaw. A boat on the first.” The cane taps once. “Then we have five days to do something the itinerary doesn't say. Use them, boy. The Court reads schedules the way I read steps — don't be where the schedule says.”`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Five days. Use one: there's a village two bays west that the winter rumors would not stop worrying at.`,go:"a4c20_fray"}]};

SC["a4c20_fray"]={t:()=>P(`The rumors said: cursed. The rumors undersold it.`)+P(`Yu-le, a fishing village of forty roofs, sits under a sky that is wrong in a manner no one in this world can see but you. Thirty feet above the drying-racks, the Weave of Heaven is TORN — not frayed, torn, a rent the length of a barge, its edges crawling with loose ends that wave like riverweed in a current of nothing. The qi of the place is bleeding upward through it, slow and steady, the world's warmth escaping through an open door.`)+P(`You see it from the boat, half a li out, and your hands start aching before you understand why: every thread you can see is under load, and the loads are wrong, and your fingers want to FIX it the way a musician's hands want to correct a detuned string.`)+P(`Below the tear, the village is dying politely. Nets rot in a day. Hens won't lay. The pond carp went belly-up under clear ice. And the old people have begun dying in their sleep, “of cold,” in a month that isn't cold — the qi of their bodies seeping up and out through a hole in the sky nobody else will ever see.`)+P(`An old fisherman meets your boat, because someone has to. “Two years it's been souring,” he says. “Priests came. Burned things. A geomancer sold us mirrors.” He looks at the water. “My wife says the village offended heaven. I keep asking her how. We're not important enough to offend anybody.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Look up. Tell him the truth: the sky over his village is torn, and nobody offended anyone.`,go:"a4c20_mend"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Say nothing yet. Walk the village first, reading the loads line by line.`,do:()=>{addIns(1);note("+1 Insight. You walk every lane before you speak. The tear is not centered on the village — it trails off upriver, thinner and older, like the end of a much longer wound. Yu-le isn't the injury. Yu-le is where the injury's edge happens to hang. The thought arrives flat and enormous: this is ONE EDGE of something.");},go:"a4c20_mend"}]};

SC["a4c20_mend"]={t:()=>P(`The mending takes you all day and most of the night, and it is the truest work you have done since the Cocoon House.`)+P(`There's no fight in it. That's what makes it the chapter of itself: just you on the drying-ground with your sleeves tied back, gold running up into the dark, reading each torn warp-line, chasing it to sound thread, knotting, sealing, moving on. Snare logic. Mend logic. The pattern-sense the basement taught you, scaled to a sky. The villagers can't see a single thing you do — to them, a foreign boy stands in their fish-yard all night with his hands raised — but around midnight the air stops tasting thin, and an hour before dawn a hen lays, and the whole village hears it and comes out of doors in their winter coats and stands there, not speaking, the warm coming back into the world around them like color into a face.`)+((G.f.bg=="music")?(P(`Near the end, exhausted, you find yourself working in time: each knot on the beat, eight bars to a warp-line, and when the last edge seals, the resolution your unfinished melody never had walks into your hands like it had only been waiting for an instrument this size.`)):(""))+((G.f.bg=="sister")?(P(`Near the end, exhausted, you catch yourself doing what you used to do on the bad nights: leaving the porch light on. One thread, looped and warm, woven shut LAST — so anything lost out there could find the seam.`)):(""))+P(`By morning it holds. The tear is closed: a long gold scar in heaven that only you will ever see.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`And then stand in the fish-yard arithmetic, because the sum is the whole act.`,req:()=>(G.insight>=12),rq:"(needs Insight 12)",do:()=>{G.f.a4_fray_read=true;},go:"a4c20_sum"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Accept the village's breakfast — every house brings something — and keep your sums to yourself.`,do:()=>{G.heart++;note("+1 Heart. Forty roofs' worth of gratitude, paid in eggs and salt fish and one grandmother's wordless, furious embrace. You let it be simple for one morning. The arithmetic will keep.");},go:"a4c20_sum"}]};

SC["a4c20_sum"]={t:()=>((G.f.a4_fray_read)?(P(`You stand where the tear was and do the sum out loud, because it deserves saying: one night's work, your whole craft, every thread you could hold — for a tear the length of a barge. The trailing edge runs upriver out of sight: this was one hem of a wound that is CONTINENTAL. The Grand Loom holds the rest shut. All of it. All the time. Whatever you think of the Court, the thing in their cellar is carrying the sky of the heartland, and it has been carrying it for four hundred years, and if it stopped, ten thousand Yu-les would happen at once. That is the Court's case. You have now seen it from inside, and it is real, and the fact that they feed people to it is a separate fact. Holding both at once is the act you're sailing into.`)):(P(`Ruan does his own sum on the boat back, bookkeeper-flat: “One village. One night. One weaver.” He looks upriver, where the trailing edge of the wound went. “However big the rest of that is, brother, it explains the Loom better than the Lady ever will. They're holding a sky shut. With people.” He closes his book. “Both of those things are true. I've been trying to make one of them cancel the other all morning. They won't.”`)))+((G.f.a3_mei_present)?(P(`Mei spent the night and the morning with Yu-le's old people, doing what salves do where weaving can't reach. On the boat back she sits beside you, takes your over-spent hands one at a time, and works the cramp out of them in silence. Then: “I'm coming. To the white city.” It is not a question and was never going to be one. “You'll argue with heaven. Someone has to keep the bodies alive while you do.” She returns your left hand. “Also, your tea is always terrible. That settles it.”`)):(""))+SYS(`The fray is real. The Loom is load-bearing. The Court is half right — and the half they're wrong about sleeps in silk hammocks. Six days until the white boat.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The loft, the last night, and the question of HOW to enter a politeness.`,go:"a4c20_embark"}]};

SC["a4c20_embark"]={t:()=>P(`Maps on the loft table, lamplight, everyone who is coming gathered around the one decision the winter left open. The Thousand Reels: the Court's seat, a white city on the upper lake. Three ways in, and the company argues them honestly.`)+((G.f.a3_court=="guest")?(P(`You accepted Madam Xian's invitation months ago, on a white deck, and the itinerary assumes it. The guest door stands open. Whether you walk through the door they built for you is tonight's whole question.`)):(""))+((G.f.a3_court=="refused")?(P(`You refused Madam Xian once, with full courtesy, and the itinerary arrived anyway — the Court treats your refusal as a scheduling preference. The guest door stands open regardless. Politeness is the net; they have never once stopped weaving it.`)):(""))+((G.f.a3_court=="defied")?(P(`You told Madam Xian it would hurt one of you, and the itinerary arrived anyway, dateless threats and all — the Court files defiance under candor and candor under charm. The guest door stands open even to you. That might be the most frightening fact on the table.`)):(""))+P(`Ruan taps the manifests: eleven halls' worth of consignment paperwork, seals, waybills, the whole grammar of the tribute trade — enough to dress you as a silk-trade auditor with cargo interests, if you'd rather arrive unannounced. And there is a third way, which no one says aloud until Granny Sho or the lamp or the late hour says it for them: consignments enter deepest of all. The Court collects weavers. A weaver could let himself be collected.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Board the white boat as the GUEST they invited. Hold their politeness to its warranty, and see everything they choose to show.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_route="guest";note("Ruan exhales through his nose, which is his whole opinion. \"Then we arrive on their schedule. I'll bring the books anyway — guests get bored.\"");},go:"a4c21_guest"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Go in as a SPY: consignment-merchant papers, Ruan's manifests, a name that isn't yours. See what the Court shows nobody.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_route="spy";note("Ruan starts forging the waybills that hour, and is frighteningly good at it. \"My master's hand,\" he says, without looking up. \"He'd be proud. I've decided not to mind.\"");},go:"a4c21_spy"},
  {id:"c2",l:`Let the Court COLLECT you: surrender as the consignment they always meant you to be, and ride their own chain into the deepest room they have.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_route="prisoner";note("Nobody speaks for a while. Then, from the stove corner or the stairwell or wherever the oldest courage in the room is sitting, quietly: \"Good. The net only shows its shape to the fish.\"");},go:"a4c21_prisoner"}]};